.TH "PVEFORGE" "1" "Sep 2026" "pveforge" "pveforge manual"

.SH NAME
pveforge-harness - Outer test-harness VM lifecycle (operator-driven)


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpveforge harness [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
The outer test-harness VM lifecycle, a Go port of hack/harness/lib.sh.

.PP
Every verb acts only on a VM in the harness range 690-699 that is a tagged
qemu member of the harness pool on the harness node, and every state decision
is made on PVE's JSON, never on its error text. The destructive tier is
confined to these verbs; the public vm command surface is unchanged.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for harness


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpveforge(1)\fP, \fBpveforge-harness-golden(1)\fP, \fBpveforge-harness-probe(1)\fP, \fBpveforge-harness-reset(1)\fP, \fBpveforge-harness-vm(1)\fP
